version: 2.0.0
description: |
  #doctor-command - Health check and diagnostics for Paradigm setup.
  Includes core setup validation and context audit checks for AI instruction file quality.
features:
  context-audit-checks:
    description: Context audit with 11 checks — stale-references, convention-contradictions, undocumented-stack, purpose-coverage, orphaned-symbols, stale-portal, instruction-vagueness, config-schema-validation, purpose-file-health, always-on-budget, warpline-guidance
    components:
      - '#context-audit'
components:
  doctor-explain:
    description: >-
      explain.ts, what paradigm doctor --explain prints. explainFindings takes every core and
      context-audit result and explains each one that failed, is missing, warned or raised an
      advisory, most severe first, with what the check looks at, what it found, every detail line
      (plain doctor shows five) and the fix. With nothing to explain it says so in one line. The
      older gap narrator still runs first for the four check names it knows.
    file: explain.ts
    tests:
      - packages/paradigm/src/commands/doctor/explain.test.ts
  doctor-honest-counts:
    description: >-
      Doctor reads its gate count, isolated symbols and .purpose file count from #project-counts,
      the module paradigm status prints from. The Gates line reports distinct declared gates
      across portal.yaml files and .purpose; the portal.yaml line reports that one file. The
      orphaned-symbols check uses the live index (premise-core findIsolatedSymbols, as paradigm
      integrity does) and no longer reads scan-index.json. Lore entries are counted under
      .paradigm/lore/entries. The stale-portal check accepts a route when source code writes its
      path as a string literal (a handler, a mounted router split across literals in one package,
      a WebSocket server path) or a route file sits at that path, and no longer accepts a file
      that merely shares a word with the route; any upper-case method, WS included, is read.
      That check is a heuristic and reports at warn level; client calls and UI component files
      are not read as handlers. When the symbol index cannot be built, doctor builds it once and
      the orphaned-symbols check reports the failure without building it again.
    file: context-audit.ts
    tests:
      - packages/paradigm/src/commands/doctor/context-audit.test.ts
      - packages/paradigm/src/core/project-counts.test.ts
  doctor-shared-file-list:
    description: "One #project-files list per `paradigm doctor` run (doctorCommand's getProjectFiles, taken on first use), shared by every check that used to walk the tree itself: the clarification-marker count (index.ts), Portal compliance (passed to checkPortalCompliance), the hook-health .purpose and anchor counts (hook-health.ts repoTraits), and the context audit's purpose-coverage, stale-portal and purpose-file-health (runContextAudit options.projectFiles; it takes its own list when called without one). Each check keeps its own skip list, applied to path segments with hasDirSegment. Inside git the list is tracked plus untracked-not-ignored files, so files in gitignored directories are not counted; in both modes .claude/worktrees/ (agent worktree copies), node_modules, .warpline, .build and .loom are left out, whether or not git ignores them (#project-files PRUNE_DIRS). A `Project file list` line says where the list came from: ok for git and for a project that is not a git repository, warn with a fix when the walk was used for any other reason (git failed or timed out, or an ignore rule matches .purpose / portal.yaml by name). That fixed purpose-file-health and purpose-coverage counting worktree copies. repoTraits still walks (to depth 4) because its job is finding nested repositories, which git does not list; that walk now prunes node_modules, .warpline, .build and .loom and still sees .claude/worktrees. Its untracked-file count is the shared list's untrackedCount (git's own count before pruning), not a second git call."
    type: utility
    files:
      - index.ts
      - context-audit.ts
      - hook-health.ts
    components:
      - '#project-files'
    tests:
      - packages/paradigm/src/commands/doctor/shared-file-list.test.ts
  doctor-fix-commands:
    description: "The commands doctor tells a user to run must exist and be the documented ones. Not initialized (.paradigm/ missing) and a missing root .purpose say 'Fix: paradigm shift' (the documented entry point, not paradigm init); a missing config.yaml says 'paradigm shift --force'. A missing or stale scan-index.json says 'paradigm reindex' (the CLI form of paradigm_reindex), and the orphaned-symbols advisory says 'run paradigm reindex first' (bare `paradigm scan` only prints usage). The closing lines name .paradigm/docs/troubleshooting.md only when that file exists, and otherwise point at `paradigm doctor --explain`."
    type: handler
    path: index.ts
    tests:
      - packages/paradigm/src/commands/doctor.test.ts
  doctor-hook-health:
    description: 7.15.2 hook-health section (hook-health.ts). Per-hook p50/p95/max wall time, kills (a start with no end older than timeout + 5 s, or a killed end) and over-budget runs from the #hook-monitor ring; repo traits that slow hooks (nested git repos/worktrees under the root, .purpose count, aspect-anchor lines, untracked-file count); plugin cache staleness (user-scope install vs marketplace/repo plugin.json, project-scope pins older than the user install, from ~/.claude/plugins/installed_plugins.json). 8.0: "Stop sections" explains the latest slow or killed Stop run from .paradigm/events/stop-timing.jsonl (top sections, the section it was stuck in; section names allowlisted by shape, Aegis M-A); "Hook version in running sessions" warns when .paradigm/.purpose-paths was written in the last 24 h, which only the pre-7.15.2 Stop hook does, i.e. a session started before a plugin update still runs the old hooks. Every non-ok line carries a concrete remedy. Advisory, never throws.
    file: hook-health.ts
    type: utility
    tags:
      - doctor
      - hooks
  doctor-learning-guard:
    description: 'Scoped learning S2 doctor lines (hook-health.ts): learningGuardChecks reports learning guard installed / not installed / foreign pre-commit hook; learnPathSkipChecks counts hook writes skipped because learn-path could not resolve (.paradigm/.sessions/learn-path-skips, written by _pm_learn_skip), per artifact, so lost data is told apart from no data.'
    type: handler
    file: packages/paradigm/src/commands/doctor/hook-health.ts
  doctor-handler:
    description: 'Core health checks for .paradigm directory, config, specs, docs, IDE files, portal, flows, lore, hooks, and habits. Warns on each Paradigm-owned git hook (.git/hooks/post-commit, pre-push) that #git-hook-state classes as outdated (below paradigm-hook-version 4, or still running `npx paradigm`), fix `paradigm hooks install`. v6.0.4 added ''info'' status for non-blocking metric surfacing (renderer only — Wave 3 wires the aspect-coverage line item that consumes it). Scoped learning S2: the classroom repeat-failure rate is grouped by home (certificationsByHome), one warn per home; liveness reads the union of the machine home and the frozen repo logs. Scoped learning S4: a Learning census info line per store (repo / user / machine counts, legacy, last write, learn-path skips), a Learning conflicts info line for Loid (repo vs user, never resolved), and the repeat-failure scoreboard labelled [population: repo|user|machine|legacy-prior]. T-2026-11-03-001: the rate uses requireExercise, so a survived row without exercise evidence counts as unproven, not resolved. Ruling 6: when the classroom-exercises ledger is empty the block says plainly Survival: no exercise events recorded yet (spec sub-phase 1): no cert can survive (NO_EXERCISE_WRITER_NOTICE from premise-core), instead of a bare n/a rate. options.homeDir (default os.homedir()) is threaded to the context audit and hook health so tests stay off the real ~/.claude.'
    type: handler
    file: index.ts
    components:
      - '#gap-narrator'
      - '#git-hook-state'
  info-status:
    description: |
      v6.0.4 CheckResult status added to the existing ok/warn/error/missing
      union. Renders as a dim '⠂' icon in chalk.gray. Surfaces metrics
      without affecting exit code or summary counters — used by line items
      that report data when no claimant is active.
    type: model
    file: index.ts
    tags:
      - doctor
      - status
      - v6.0.4
  context-audit:
    description: '11 context quality checks for AI instruction files (CLAUDE.md, .cursorrules, AGENTS.md). Check 11 warpline-guidance (T-2026-11-12-001, advisory): when #warpline-detect finds Warpline (and guidance is not off), CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md that exist must carry the <!-- warpline:begin --> block, and a project with generated Cursor rules must have paradigm-warpline.mdc; otherwise an advisory: run `paradigm sync` if Paradigm generates these files, or `warpline init` to add only the block. Markers match as whole lines outside fenced code; two blocks or unpaired markers get their own malformed advisory. A CLAUDE.md that is a directory is skipped (loadInstructionFiles also skips non-files). Silent (no result) without Warpline. Check 10 always-on-budget (advisory, #always-on-budget) emits one result per surface (claude-code, cursor, agents-md) with chars and estimated tokens (chars/4) per file as details, advisory (never warn or error, so doctor and shift stay healthy; Judge B1) when the surface''s Paradigm-generated total exceeds context.always-on-max-chars (default 12000, a starting estimate), plus an ok census line for user-owned text (~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, MEMORY.md, non-Paradigm skills and rules; MCP tool schemas not measured) that is never warned on. runContextAudit accepts options.homeDir for tests. purpose-coverage skips gitignored source dirs (purpose-core filterGitIgnored; release/ by name outside git) so build and release output never counts, and counts a dir as covered only by the shared #purpose-coverage rule (own .purpose or a documenting ancestor; placeholders never count) (T-2026-10-27-003).'
    type: utility
    tags:
      - feature
      - context-quality
    file: context-audit.ts
  agent-audit:
    description: 'v7.9.1 (TD-2026-09-26-846) auditAgents(rootDir, {globalDir?}) — pure check behind doctor''s "Agent profile keys" (warn on keys outside a local KNOWN_AGENT_KEYS copy; info when `behaviors:` is present but unread until skills Phase 1) and "Roster dispatchability" (warn on active roster ids with no project/global .agent and no agents.yaml entry, or benched on the roster; fix = paradigm agent sync-global or deactivate). Scans project .agent files plus roster-relevant global ones. v7.10.0 (Skills Phase 1): `skills` is a known key; skillMigrations() scans project + global SKILL.md provenance.migratedFrom and auditAgents returns migratedBehaviors, which doctor renders as info lines "<file> `behaviors.<block>` migrated to skill <id>".'
    type: utility
    file: agent-audit.ts
    tags:
      - doctor
      - agent-identity
  mcp-portability-audit:
    description: 'auditMcpPortability(rootDir) — scans the committed project MCP configs (.mcp.json, .cursor/mcp.json, .cline/mcp.json) for a server whose cwd or an args entry is an absolute path (POSIX or Windows; ${...} placeholders pass). Doctor renders "MCP config portability" warn (with `paradigm sync` as the fix when only the paradigm server is affected) or ok. Advisory — never fails doctor. 2x-engineers report 2026-11-01.'
    type: utility
    file: mcp-portability-audit.ts
    tags:
      - doctor
      - mcp-config
  legacy-names-audit:
    description: 'v7.13.0 (T-2026-09-26-005, MCP surface cut) auditLegacyToolNames(rootDir) — scans CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, .cursor/rules/** and .claude/settings{,.local}.json permissions.{allow,deny,ask} for renamed pre-7.13 `paradigm_<family>_<op>` tool names (anchors and same-name entries excluded). Driven by #legacy-tool-map (single source of truth, imported from paradigm-mcp). Doctor renders "Legacy tool names (permissions)" warn (dead allowlist entries re-prompt) and "Legacy tool names" warn with the family({op}) replacement; ok when clean. Advisory — never fails doctor.'
    type: utility
    file: legacy-names-audit.ts
    tags:
      - doctor
      - mcp-surface
      - v7.13.0
  doctor-history-audit:
    description: 'History storage audit (history-audit.ts, T-2026-11-06-001). historyAuditChecks(root): warn when the post-commit hook (worktree-aware hooks dir via `git rev-parse --git-path hooks`) is a Paradigm hook below v4 (writes tracked history, tree dirty after every commit), when .paradigm/history/index.yaml is still tracked, or when .gitattributes lacks the log.jsonl merge=union block; info when legacy ids occur more than once (they resolve as <id>@<sha7>); ok otherwise. Fix: `paradigm sync && paradigm hooks install`, then commit. Git via execFileSync, never throws.'
    type: utility
    file: history-audit.ts
    components:
      - '#git-hook-state'
      - '#session-markers-gitignore'
    tags:
      - doctor
      - history
